cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, together with the guidelines and validation references it reproduces."
title: "Bioequivalence Lab: bilingual NCA and bioequivalence analysis in the browser"
abstract: >-
  Arabic/English web application that runs Python engines in the browser (Pyodide) for
  non-compartmental analysis and bioequivalence: average BE (subject-contrast and fixed-effects
  models), EMA ABEL, FDA RSABE and NTI methods, multi-treatment, multi-group and two-stage designs,
  endogenous substances, potency correction, and power and sample size, under an ICH M13A / EMA / FDA
  framework and an SFDA / GCC (DS-G-010 V3.1) framework. Research and teaching use; not validated for
  regulatory submissions.
type: software
